Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions (From My Experience)
Hey LinkedIn fam 👋,
While preparing for upcoming DevOps interviews, I realized that scenario-based questions are becoming the new norm—especially for mid-level roles (5+ years of experience).
I’m sharing a collection of real-world questions I’ve faced (or seen commonly asked) to help fellow DevOps professionals gear up. Hope this helps someone out there! 🚀
🧩 Jenkins / CI-CD Scenarios
🔹 Jenkins pipeline works in staging but fails in production — how do you debug?
 🔹 Job stuck at “Waiting for executor” — what do you check?
 🔹 How to roll back a failed deployment?
 🔹 How to prevent accidental prod deployments from feature branches?

🐳 Docker Scenarios
🔹 A container keeps restarting — how do you troubleshoot?
 🔹 Image size is too large — how do you optimize it?
 🔹 Best practices for handling secrets in Docker?
🔹 Difference between entrypoint and cmd

☸️ Kubernetes Scenarios
🔹 Pod stuck in CrashLoopBackOff — where do you begin?
 🔹 Rolling back a failed production deployment?
 🔹 Making a service cluster-internal only — how?
 🔹 Secret rotation without downtime — how would you approach it?

☁️ AWS / Cloud Infra
🔹 EC2 instance is unresponsive — first things to check?
 🔹 Performing zero-downtime deployments in AWS?
 🔹 Autoscaling setup based on CPU usage — how?

🐧 Linux Scenarios
🔹 Disk space is full on a production server — what do you do?
 🔹 A process is consuming high CPU — how do you troubleshoot it?
 🔹 A server is not reachable via SSH — how would you diagnose it?
 🔹 How do you schedule regular backups using cron?
